      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bamberg%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Evidence suggests that the Edisto tribe of the Muskogian Indians once lived and hunted in the area known as Bamberg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofbambergsc.gov/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The building of a water tank for the Charleston-Hamburg railroad in 1832 helped start the city of Bamberg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofbambergsc.gov/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Carlisle Military School was founded in Bamberg in 1893 as a branch of Wofford College.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
